From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: never send TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR, and probe
 firmware liveness after init

The kernel enum airoha_npu_wlan_set_cmd has 34 entries (0..33) while the
NPU firmware SET_WAIT command table has only 31 (0..30) in both the Kite
and Eagle variants.  Command 32 (TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR) is therefore rejected
with mailbox status ERROR.

Ignoring the -EINVAL (previous approach) lets the bind succeed, but the
firmware then stops completing mailbox transactions entirely: the
MacTable DEL_STA sent on station association times out with -ETIMEDOUT,
so Wi-Fi offload still never works.  Reloading mt7915e afterwards makes
even airoha_npu_wlan_init_memory() fail, i.e. the firmware stays silent
once it has seen the out-of-range command.

Do not send the command at all.  The firmware has no handler for it and
never uses the tx-bufid region.

Also add a post-init probe: query WLAN_FUNC_GET_WAIT_NPU_VERSION right
after init and log the result, so "firmware alive after init" can be told
apart from "firmware silent" from dmesg alone.

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -539,10 +539,15 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	cmd = WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR;
-	err = airoha_npu_wlan_set_reserved_memory(npu, 0, "tx-bufid", cmd);
-	if (err)
-		return err;
+	/* WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_TX_BUF_CHECK_ADDR (32) is past the end of the
+	 * NPU firmware SET_WAIT command table, which holds 31 entries (0..30)
+	 * in both the Kite and Eagle firmware variants.  The firmware answers
+	 * the command with mailbox status ERROR and then stops completing
+	 * mailbox transactions altogether: every later command -- e.g. the
+	 * MacTable DEL_STA issued when a station associates -- times out with
+	 * -ETIMEDOUT and Wi-Fi offload never works.  Never send it: the
+	 * firmware has no handler for it and never uses the tx-bufid region.
+	 */
 
 	cmd = WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_PKT_BUF_ADDR;
 	err = airoha_npu_wlan_set_reserved_memory(npu, 0, "pkt", cmd);
@@ -567,7 +567,25 @@
 			return err;
 	}
 
-	cmd = WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_IS_FORCE_TO_CPU;
-	return airoha_npu_wlan_msg_send(npu, 0, cmd, &val, sizeof(val),
-					GFP_KERNEL);
+	cmd = WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_IS_FORCE_TO_CPU;
+	err = airoha_npu_wlan_msg_send(npu, 0, cmd, &val, sizeof(val),
+				       GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
+
+	/* Post-init sanity check: is the firmware still completing mailbox
+	 * transactions?  -ETIMEDOUT here means the firmware went silent right
+	 * after init and offload cannot work at all.
+	 */
+	{
+		u32 ver = 0;
+		int r;
+
+		r = airoha_npu_wlan_msg_get(npu, 0, WLAN_FUNC_GET_WAIT_NPU_VERSION,
+					    &ver, sizeof(ver), GFP_KERNEL);
+		dev_info(npu->dev, "NPU post-init check: version query ret=%d ver=0x%x\n",
+			 r, ver);
+	}
+
+	return 0;
 }
